<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlement set for a self-signed build.

  The shipped Minis.entitlements asks for nine capabilities that a free-tier
  Personal Team profile, an ad-hoc certificate, or most third-party signing
  services cannot grant. A profile that requests them fails signature
  validation; one that silently drops them produces a binary that used to
  crash on the first container lookup.

  This file is the empty set. Use it when building locally with a free Apple
  ID:

    xcodebuild -project src/ios/Minis.xcodeproj -scheme Minis \
      -configuration Release -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' \
      DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=<your team id> \
      CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS=src/ios/Personal.entitlements build

  or point each target at it in Signing & Capabilities. The unsigned CI
  artifact needs nothing from this file — it carries no entitlements blob at
  all, and the signing tool on the device side supplies whatever its profile
  allows.

  What degrades, and how:

    App Groups        Files-app visibility of shared/ skills/ memory/ is gone
                      and the share extension cannot hand attachments over.
                      Every path still resolves: SharedContainerStore
                      .sharedDirectory(_:) falls back to Application Support.
                      This is the only entry that used to crash the app.
    iCloud/CloudKit   Backup and sync unavailable. Sync is off on a clean
                      install, so nothing attempts a connection.
    HealthKit         health offload tools report unavailable.
    HomeKit           home offload tools report unavailable.
    NFC               reader unavailable.
    WeatherKit        weather tool reports unavailable.
    aps-environment   no push. Nothing registers for remote notifications.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
